# Government Service Request & Approval Portal

I rebuilt this project around a common operational challenge: a process can technically work through email and spreadsheets while still creating unnecessary delays, inconsistent records, weak accountability, and limited visibility.

> All organizations, users, requests, documents, and performance measures in this project are fictional.

## Challenge

A fictional government organization receives service requests through multiple email accounts, static forms, and spreadsheets. Required information varies by requester, approvals depend on manual follow-up, supporting documents become separated from the request, and users have no consistent way to understand status. Meanwhile, leadership cannot easily measure workload, turnaround time, bottlenecks, or overdue actions.

## Solution

I designed a centralized request and approval portal using Power Apps/Power Pages, Power Automate, Dataverse or SharePoint, and Power BI. The solution creates one controlled lifecycle from initial request through triage, review, fulfillment, and closure.

