## Workflow Architecture

1. **Request Submission** — requester enters required information, attaches evidence, and saves or submits.
2. **Triage & Assignment** — validation and business rules route the request to the appropriate team.
3. **Review & Approval** — authorized reviewers approve, reject, return, reassign, or escalate while decisions are recorded.
4. **Fulfillment & Closure** — the assigned team documents resolution, satisfies completion criteria, and closes the request.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    R[Requester] --> APP[Power Apps / Power Pages]
    APP --> DATA[(Dataverse / SharePoint)]
    APP --> FLOW[Power Automate]
    FLOW --> REV[Review / Approval]
    REV --> FUL[Fulfillment]
    DATA --> BI[Power BI]
    FLOW --> COMMS[Teams / Outlook]
```

## Why This Solution Fits the Challenge

The strongest part of the design is not the form itself. Rather, the value comes from converting an informal sequence of emails into a governed state-based process. Each transition has an owner, a decision, a timestamp, and a next action. Consequently, operational work becomes measurable without requiring a second reporting process to reconstruct what happened.

